# Review required on the paths where a silent break costs a competition day.
#
# Deliberately narrow. Broad code-owner rules stall a volunteer team; these four
# areas are the ones where a mistake is invisible until the robot is on the field.
#
# WHO: one owner, the mentor who does the plumbing. GitHub never requests a review
# from a PR's own author, so a plumbing PR the owner opens requests nobody, and one
# anyone else opens requests the owner. That is the gate we actually want: nothing changes the
# locked versions, CI or the RC configs without the person maintaining them seeing it.
#
# HISTORY (27 Sep 2026): this file used to list all six programming-mentor handles
# on every path. Nearly all plumbing PRs are the owner's own, so each one
# auto-requested review from five mentors who were not working on it (#40, #56,
# #70, #86, #87) - and every one merged without those reviews, because branch
# protection does not require code-owner review. The requests were pure noise, and
# noise trains people to ignore the requests that matter. Options rejected:
#   - Delete this file: loses the one useful effect, being pinged when someone
#     else touches the locked set.
#   - Open as draft: drafts only defer the request to "Ready for review".
#   - Keep all six, remove reviewers by hand each time: the notification has
#     already gone out by then.
# The mentor pool the season-standup skill assigns from used to be read off this
# file; it now lives in .claude/skills/season-standup/SKILL.md.
#
# To pull another mentor into a specific PR, request them by hand - that ping
# means something.
#
# NOTE: this file only has teeth once branch protection on `master` is set to
# "Require review from Code Owners". Until then it is advisory. Do not turn that
# on while one person owns everything: the owner could never merge their own PRs.
#
# A misspelled handle, or one without repository access, silently matches NOBODY
# rather than erroring. Check changes here against the collaborator list by eye.

# Dependency versions are a locked set - see TeamCode/README.md
/build.dependencies.gradle   @dustinhans
/TeamCode/build.gradle       @dustinhans
/build.common.gradle         @dustinhans
/gradle/wrapper/             @dustinhans

# CI and dependency automation
/.github/workflows/          @dustinhans
/.github/dependabot.yml      @dustinhans

# Robot hardware configuration - the XML and the constants must agree
/TeamCode/src/main/res/xml/   @dustinhans

# Upstream code we do not patch
/FtcRobotController/         @dustinhans
